	It is worth noting, however, that if you have bunches of stuff you would 
like to identify, but you really really want to know if the amulet you got is 
strangulation or lifesaving, and whether or not the ring is hunger or conflict, 
and then, what is NR 9, and then, just how many pluses DOES Excalibur currently 
have on it; if you just hit return, you will have to choose AS you reach them.  
And if you only get two choices out of it, Excalibur will probably pop up first, 
and then the scroll, then the ring, and then the amulet.  (Usually is order you 
picked them up...)  If, however, you choose "=?)    as the order, you will 
identify amulets first, then if you have any more identifications left you will 
do rings, then scrolls, then weapons.  It is FAR more efficient to do it this 
way.  You will rarely waste id's this way, whereas if you do the default order,
you will go through, but if you pass the ring by because you HAVE to know what 
the amulet is first, you don't get to go back.  Consequently, stating the order 
should ALWAYS be done.

	Second, when dropping stuff, or picking stuff up, if you know you want 
all of what you specify, type an a   at the end, and it will pick them all up 
(unless you run out of weight allowance first) without asking you to verify each 
one.  (if you have just killed a cockatrice, don't do this on %s...)


